---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import PageAnchors from "@/components/layout/PageAnchors.astro";
import { getNavLink } from "@/lib/blog-helpers";
import { site } from "@/data/focuslab";
---

<PageLayout
	meta={{
		title: "Jobs",
		description:
			"Working at Focus Lab, a small independent product studio in Islamabad. Open roles, how we work, and what we look for in a hire.",
	}}
>
	<div class="page">
		<div class="page__headline">
			<p class="page__kicker">Jobs</p>
			<h1>Working at Focus Lab</h1>
			<p>
				Take a look at our current openings, sign up to be notified about future ones, and learn
				what it's like to work here.
			</p>
			<PageAnchors
				anchors={[
					{ id: "who-we-are", label: "Who we are" },
					{ id: "who-you-are", label: "Who you are" },
					{ id: "how-we-work", label: "How we work" },
				]}
			/>
		</div>

		<div class="jobs">
			<div class="jobs__container">
				<div class="jobs__job">
					<p><em>We don't have any open positions right now.</em></p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="signup signup--jobs content">
				<h2>Sign up to be notified</h2>
				<p>
					If you'd like to be notified about job openings, sign up below, or <a
						href={getNavLink("/feed/jobs.xml")}>grab the RSS feed</a
					>. We will never share your email, or use it for any other purpose.
				</p>
				<form data-signup data-mailto={site.email} data-subject="Focus Lab jobs" novalidate>
					<input
						type="email"
						name="email"
						aria-label="Email address"
						placeholder="you@example.com"
						spellcheck="false"
						autocomplete="email"
						required
					/>
					<button class="button button--theme" type="submit">Sign up</button>
				</form>
			</div>

			<div class="jobs__content content content--jobs">
				<h2 id="who-we-are">Who we are</h2>
				<p class="lede">
					A small studio that builds its own products and answers to the people who use them.
				</p>
				<p>
					Focus Lab is a product studio based in Islamabad. We design, build, and run our own
					software: Urbanevents for events and ticketing, Workproof for a calm record of the work,
					and Fixer, which triages production errors and opens draft pull requests. Once in a while
					we partner with a team when the fit is right.
				</p>
				<p>
					We work with Shopify, Cloudflare, Framer, Astro, React, TypeScript, Node.js, PostgreSQL,
					Stripe, and OpenAI or Anthropic. We pick tools that let us ship quickly and keep running
					what we build.
				</p>
				<p>We're independent and self-funded, which is why the terms below look the way they do.</p>

				<h2 id="who-you-are">Who you are</h2>
				<p class="lede">Rock star? Pass. Thoughtful and self-directed? Let's talk.</p>
				<ol class="numbered">
					<li>
						<div class="numbered__body">
							<h3 class="numbered__title">You own the whole thing.</h3>
							<p>
								You're a manager of one. You can take a rough goal, break it down, and ship without
								someone checking in on you every day.
							</p>
						</div>
					</li>
					<li>
						<div class="numbered__body">
							<h3 class="numbered__title">You write plainly.</h3>
							<p>
								You say what you mean, and you communicate early — especially when something isn't
								working.
							</p>
						</div>
					</li>
					<li>
						<div class="numbered__body">
							<h3 class="numbered__title">You go to the end of it.</h3>
							<p>
								You're comfortable owning a product from a first sketch to a running service. When
								something breaks, you look into it.
							</p>
						</div>
					</li>
					<li>
						<div class="numbered__body">
							<h3 class="numbered__title">You care about craft and outcome.</h3>
							<p>
								Not just the ticket. You'd rather ship the right thing late than the wrong thing on
								time.
							</p>
						</div>
					</li>
				</ol>
				<p>
					We don't care where you studied, where you've worked, or whether you finished a degree. We
					care about what you can do now, how you'll grow, and how you treat the people you work
					with.
				</p>

				<h2 id="how-we-work">How we work</h2>
				<p class="lede">A calm, low-distraction environment where you can do your best work.</p>
				<p>
					We work in small, independent teams and give people room to own their part. Fewer
					meetings, less email, fewer interruptions.
				</p>

				<table class="ledger">
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Day</th>
							<td>Eight hours. That's the whole expectation.</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Week</th>
							<td>Forty hours, and we protect them.</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Meetings</th>
							<td> A weekly one, kept short. Everything else is a document. </td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Location</th>
							<td>
								Remote-friendly, with a home base in Islamabad. We gather in person when it's worth
								it.
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Company</th>
							<td>
								Independent and self-funded. We make more than we spend, and we keep the team small
								on purpose.
							</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>

				<p>
					That last row is the one that matters most. Being able to move fast, stay close to the
					work, and hold on to the details is a direct consequence of nobody having to answer to a
					board. If that sounds like you, we'd like to hear from you.
				</p>

				<blockquote class="pull">
					<p>
						Work isn't war. Nobody here is fighting a battle they have to win by Saturday, and we
						hire for people who'd rather be right in March than loud in June.
					</p>
					<cite>Focus Lab</cite>
				</blockquote>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</PageLayout>
